# Approach 2 — Binary Trie

Insert all numbers into a binary Trie.

For every number `x`, find the number in the Trie that maximizes:

```text
x XOR y
```

At every bit, prefer:

```text
1 - currentBit
```

### Java

```java
class BinaryTrie {

    static class Node {
        Node[] child = new Node[2];
    }

    private final Node root = new Node();

    void insert(int num) {

        Node node = root;

        for (int bit = 31; bit >= 0; bit--) {

            int b = (num >>> bit) & 1;

            if (node.child[b] == null)
                node.child[b] = new Node();

            node = node.child[b];
        }
    }

    int maxXor(int num) {

        Node node = root;

        int result = 0;

        for (int bit = 31; bit >= 0; bit--) {

            int b = (num >>> bit) & 1;

            int opposite = b ^ 1;

            if (node.child[opposite] != null) {

                result |= (1 << bit);

                node = node.child[opposite];

            } else {
                node = node.child[b];
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}

public static int findMaximumXOR(int[] nums) {

    BinaryTrie trie = new BinaryTrie();

    for (int num : nums)
        trie.insert(num);

    int answer = 0;

    for (int num : nums)
        answer = Math.max(answer, trie.maxXor(num));

    return answer;
}
```

