# 5. Longest Word With All Prefixes

**a2z-461 — Longest Word with All Prefixes · Medium** 

Given:

```text
words = [
    "n",
    "ni",
    "nin",
    "ninj",
    "ninja"
]
```

`ninja` qualifies because:

```text
n
ni
nin
ninj
ninja
```

all exist.

---

## Approach — Trie

Each Trie node stores:

```text
isEnd
```

meaning a complete word ends there.

For a candidate word:

```text
ninja
```

walk through:

```text
n
ni
nin
ninj
ninja
```

At every node:

```text
isEnd == true
```

must hold.

---

### Java

```java
class TrieNode {

    TrieNode[] child = new TrieNode[26];

    boolean isEnd;
}

public static String longestWord(String[] words) {

    TrieNode root = new TrieNode();

    for (String word : words) {

        TrieNode node = root;

        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {

            int index = c - 'a';

            if (node.child[index] == null)
                node.child[index] = new TrieNode();

            node = node.child[index];
        }

        node.isEnd = true;
    }

    String answer = "";

    for (String word : words) {

        TrieNode node = root;

        boolean valid = true;

        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {

            node = node.child[c - 'a'];

            if (!node.isEnd) {
                valid = false;
                break;
            }
        }

        if (valid) {

            if (word.length() > answer.length()
                    || (word.length() == answer.length()
                    && word.compareTo(answer) < 0)) {

                answer = word;
            }
        }
    }

    return answer;
}
```

