# 6. Trie Implementation — Advanced Operations

**a2z-460 — Trie Implementation and Advanced Operations · Hard** 

Typical operations:

```text
insert(word)
search(word)
startsWith(prefix)
erase(word)
countWordsEqualTo(word)
countWordsStartingWith(prefix)
```

For interview preparation, this is the implementation worth memorizing.

---

## Java

```java
class Trie {

    static class Node {

        Node[] child = new Node[26];

        int prefixCount;

        int wordCount;
    }

    private final Node root = new Node();

    public void insert(String word) {

        Node node = root;

        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {

            int index = c - 'a';

            if (node.child[index] == null)
                node.child[index] = new Node();

            node = node.child[index];

            node.prefixCount++;
        }

        node.wordCount++;
    }

    public int countWordsEqualTo(String word) {

        Node node = findNode(word);

        return node == null ? 0 : node.wordCount;
    }

    public int countWordsStartingWith(String prefix) {

        Node node = findNode(prefix);

        return node == null ? 0 : node.prefixCount;
    }

    public void erase(String word) {

        Node node = root;

        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {

            int index = c - 'a';

            node = node.child[index];

            node.prefixCount--;
        }

        node.wordCount--;
    }

    public boolean search(String word) {
        return countWordsEqualTo(word) > 0;
    }

    public boolean startsWith(String prefix) {
        return countWordsStartingWith(prefix) > 0;
    }

    private Node findNode(String s) {

        Node node = root;

        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {

            int index = c - 'a';

            if (node.child[index] == null)
                return null;

            node = node.child[index];
        }

        return node;
    }
}
```

